contrast_pool_s2026.pt                # 0.8515 solo (-0.0119 vs the calib_dense_hold control, -0.0032 vs its own contrast_dense control), and seat value 0.0000: the honest greedy over the roster peaks at 0.8763/20 seats with or without it, identical to four decimals. Declined on BOTH rulers, which is why this is a decline and not a deferral - contrast_dense is on the roster precisely because it fails the solo ruler and passes the seat one. Re-open by answering the argument: the widened pool refuted the batch-size explanation on measurement (loss 5.859 vs 3.605 at e0, so 96 keys per anchor really were supplied), so a re-open needs a DIFFERENT representation term, not this one with another weight. See experiments/README.md 2026-08-30 and knee-agrj.
swin_supervised_s2026.pt              # 0.8331 solo (CONVERGED at epoch 6; epochs 7-11 declined) and seat value -0.0012 against greedyseat_v1: the roster of 7 scores 0.8763 and this one makes it 0.8751, band [-0.0020, -0.0003], best possible swap -0.0013. Declined despite being the most DECORRELATED member the project owns — nearest-neighbour 0.8346 against seated members' 0.8772-0.9225 — which is the finding in the decline: maximal diversity cannot pay for a 0.020 solo deficit. Re-open by answering the argument, and the answer is already armed: knee-94ec found that block discovery took the longest ModuleList and so opened only layers.2.blocks.12-17, leaving stage 3 (the top of the network, 1024 wide) frozen for the whole run. swin_wholetop (knee-tsiz) re-runs this recipe byte-identical on the fixed discovery. Re-open on THAT number, not on this one.
